      "output_tokens": 256,
      "output_text": "A hash table, also known as a hash map, is a data structure that implements an associative array abstract data type, a structure that can map keys to values. It uses a hash function to compute an index into an array of buckets or slots, from which the desired value can be found.\n\n### Key Components of a Hash Table:\n1. **Hash Function**: A function that takes an input (key) and returns an index (hash value) in the array. The goal is to distribute the keys uniformly across the array to minimize collisions.\n2. **Array (or List)**: An array of buckets or linked lists. Each bucket can store one or more key-value pairs.\n3. **Collision Resolution**: Techniques to handle situations where two different keys hash to the same index (collision). Common methods include chaining (using a linked list) and open addressing (probing for an empty slot).\n\n### Operations Made Fast:\nThe primary operations that are made fast in a hash table are:\n\n1. **Insertion**: Adding a new key-value pair to the hash table. This operation is typically O(1) on average, assuming a good hash function and a low collision rate.\n2. **Search**: Finding a key-value pair by its key. This operation is also O",
